# Live docs content and ownership

- Preserve product law. Label [Product law], [Selected], [Research], and [Technical analysis] separately. Do not collapse a research verdict into a shipped claim.
- Preserve the near-term live-docs priorities: HTML-first catalog of every public node, option, and feature; stable `kindId` URLs; editor info icon deep links; bot/AI + SEO + GEO twins (`llms.txt`, markdown, JSON); existing CI + GitHub Pages as the publish path.
- Preserve the long-term vision: docs as a protocol the canvas, in-page agent, VS Code host, and a future native attach path all speak. Same record, many projections. No second Branch article.
- Treat the public Pages site as the near-term user-facing surface; treat in-app F1 / markdown-twin panel and native-host hovers as later viewers of the same files.
- Keep canvas / node / option / pin as source of truth. Generated tables come from `syntax-registry` `list()`. Overlays must not invent ports, kinds, or language APIs.
- Record leftover honesty: if Generate would print `(x)`, the live page says leftover first. Do not pretty-print a missing emit.
- Keep client-first: no docs microservice, no product accounts to read help, no secret search keys required to open a page.
- Keep playground as progressive enhancement, not the only copy. JS-off still reads definition + tables.
- Founders / product own vision, acceptance ("info icon opens the kind URL"), and the protocol bet. Technical writing owns schema, SSG, sitemap, and CI gates.
- A selected direction (SSG catalog from registry) may precede a full overlay set. Do not claim the catalog is complete without coverage evidence. Do not claim GEO/SEO works without real HTML in the Pages artifact.
